# Production build settings.
#
# WHY THE ANON KEY IS IN THE REPOSITORY. It is public by design. Vite
# compiles every VITE_ variable into the bundle, so this exact string is
# already served to every visitor of the site -- committing it to a private
# repository is strictly less exposure than deploying it, which is the whole
# point of the key. It carries no privileges of its own: every row-level
# policy applies to it exactly as it would to an anonymous caller.
#
# It is here because passing it by hand went wrong twice -- once arriving as
# bullet characters from a masked copy, which built a client that could not
# reach anything, and once as the service_role key, which would have
# published full database access to the internet had the build not refused.
# A value that must never vary is not worth retyping.
#
# THE service_role KEY MUST NEVER APPEAR IN THIS FILE, or in any VITE_
# variable. It bypasses every policy. It belongs in Key Vault, read by the
# API tier, and nowhere a browser can see.
# Sign-in talks to Supabase DIRECTLY.
#
# api/lib/authProxy.mjs exists to put this hop behind the API instead, for
# the networks that answer NXDOMAIN for <ref>.supabase.co. It is written and
# unit-tested, but it does NOT work deployed: with SUPABASE_URL set, the
# outbound fetch takes the worker down before the handler's own catch can
# report anything, and the app's logs were not reachable from where it was
# built. Proven current by removing the setting, which produced this
# module's own 503 -- so the code runs; the fetch is what does not survive.
#
# Pointing this at the proxy would break sign-in for EVERYONE rather than
# for one network, so it stays direct until the proxy is proven end to end.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://sdhprpbfazpyghjepzpt.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6InNkaHBycGJmYXpweWdoamVwenB0Iiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJpYXQiOjE3ODQ5OTY5MDMsImV4cCI6MjEwMDU3MjkwM30.HURLe79g1EX8vuMCRTbaBRhxd7JLsOINBptHjw_0LPI

# The cutover switches.
VITE_API_BASE=/api
VITE_BLOB_STORAGE=on

# Sign-in with Microsoft Entra ID (app registration "TechZoid CRM").
# None of these are secrets: a client id, a tenant id and a scope are all
# public by design and already visible to anyone who opens the sign-in page.
# Remove VITE_AUTH to fall back to Supabase sign-in.
VITE_AUTH=entra
VITE_ENTRA_CLIENT_ID=be646578-2d72-46cf-987d-a86d6393e1b3
VITE_ENTRA_TENANT_ID=1d063589-6565-42de-8055-92aca1128f35
VITE_ENTRA_API_SCOPE=api://be646578-2d72-46cf-987d-a86d6393e1b3/access_as_user
